+# EKA2L1 PortMaster / H700 port notes
+
+## Current architecture
+
+- Fresh upstream EKA2L1 core.
+- Qt is excluded when `EKA2L1_PORTMASTER=ON`.
+- SDL2 owns the native fullscreen window.
+- The graphics context is requested as native OpenGL ES 3.x before window creation.
+- `gl_context_sdl2` uses `SDL_GL_CreateContext`, `SDL_GL_SwapWindow` and `SDL_GL_GetProcAddress`.
+- No GLX/X11/Wayland requirement in the PortMaster target.
+- System CA trust uses mbedTLS and the host CA bundle instead of Qt Network.
+
+## Dual-stick work imported conceptually from EKA2L1-DualStick
+
+The Android-specific Java code was not copied into Linux.  Its useful input ideas
+were reimplemented in the common SDL2 controller backend:
+
+- real dead-zone before normalisation;
+- independent left and right sticks;
+- eight digital stick directions exposed to EKA2L1's existing button map;
+- press/release hysteresis to avoid chatter near the threshold;
+- stable controller identity via SDL joystick instance IDs;
+- deterministic H700 controller mapping, including both sticks, stick clicks and triggers.
+
+SDL_GameController performs the platform-axis canonicalisation that the Android
+DualStick code had to implement manually (RX/RY versus Z/RZ).
+
+## H700 graphics rule
+
+Never try desktop OpenGL first on the legacy Mali/fbdev stack. Request an ES profile
+before SDL creates the OpenGL window. The current target asks for GLES 3.0, matching
+upstream EKA2L1's `#version 300 es` shaders while remaining compatible with Mali's
+higher ES 3.x capability.
+
+## Next iteration
+
+1. Cross-configure against the real H700 sysroot/toolchain.
+2. Fix compile/link gaps from missing submodules and target libraries.
+3. Produce an ARM64 probe/runtime binary.
+4. Run on-device graphics + controller diagnostics before enabling launcher/menu work.
