+# EKA2L1 PortMaster / H700 — iteration 2
+
+This branch adds a Qt-free SDL2/native-GLES frontend to current EKA2L1 for ARM64 PortMaster handhelds, with H700 as the primary target.
+
+Main changes: `EKA2L1_PORTMASTER`, SDL2 window/context, GLES 3 requested before window creation, no GLX/X11/Wayland in this mode, SDL-based GL procedure loading, Qt-free POSIX TLS trust, CLI launch by Symbian UID, and dual-stick input refinements inspired by `Andiweli/EKA2L1-DualStick` (deadzone, hysteresis, independent left/right digital directions and stable triggers).
+
+The supplied GitHub ZIP has 40 empty submodule directories. Run:
+
+```sh
+./scripts/fetch_portmaster_submodules.sh
+```
+
+The script uses `SUBMODULES.lock` to restore the exact gitlink revisions for upstream commit `11f5b6cd141c0884a130ee45743f1f5e17bb1783` even when the source tree itself has no `.git` directory.
+
+Build entry point:
+
+```sh
+cmake -S . -B build-h700 -DEKA2L1_PORTMASTER=ON -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
+  -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=/path/to/h700-toolchain.cmake
+cmake --build build-h700 --target eka2l1_portmaster -j4
+```
